      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the number of distinct values in the list \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{1^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor, \\left\\lfloor \\frac{2^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor, \\left\\lfloor \\frac{3^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor, \\dots, \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1000^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\).\n\nFirst, let's understand the expression \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor\\). This expression represents the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(\\frac{n^2}{1000}\\). We need to determine the smallest integer \\(k\\) such that \\(\\left\\lfloor \\frac{k^2}{1000} \\right\\rfloor = n\\), which means \\(\\left\\{ \\frac{k^2}{1000} \\right\\} = n - \\epsilon\\) for some \\(\\epsilon > 0\\), where \\(\\{x\\}\\) denotes the fractional part of \\(x\\).\n\nThis implies:\n\\[\n\\frac{k^2}{1000} - \\epsilon < n \\leq \\frac{k^2}{1000} + \\epsilon.\n\\]\nSince the fractional part \\(\\{x\\}\\) is bounded by 1, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{k^2}{1000} - n < \\epsilon \\leq \\frac{k^2}{1000} - n + 1.\n\\]\nFor \\(\\epsilon > 0\\), the only way for \\(\\frac{k^2}{1000} - \\epsilon < n\\) is if \\(\\epsilon\\) is very small and can be considered negligible. Therefore, we need:\n\\[\n\\frac{k^2}{1000} - n < \\frac{1}{2},\n\\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{k^2}{1000} < n + \\frac{1}{2}.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\nk^2 < 1000 \\left(n + \\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 1000n + 500.\n\\]\nTaking the square root of both sides, we get:\n\\[\nk < \\sqrt{1000n + 500}.\n\\]\nThe smallest integer \\(k\\) is then:\n\\[\nk = \\left\\lceil \\sqrt{1000n + 500} \\right\\rceil - 1.\n\\]\nTo determine the number of distinct values, we need to find the range of \\(k\\) as \\(n\\) varies from 1 to 999. The smallest value of \\(k\\) when \\(n = 1\\) is:\n\\[\nk = \\left\\lceil \\sqrt{1000 + 500} \\right\\rceil - 1 = \\left\\lceil \\sqrt{1500} \\right\\rceil - 1 = 39 - 1 = 38.\n\\]\nThe largest value of \\(k\\) when \\(n = 999\\) is:\n\\[\nk = \\left\\lceil \\sqrt{999000 + 500} \\right\\rceil - 1 = \\left\\lceil \\sqrt{999500} \\right\\rceil - 1 = 999 - 1 = 998.\n\\]\nTherefore, \\(k\\) ranges from 38 to 998. The number of integers in this range is:\n\\[\n998 - 38 + 1 = 961.\n\\]\nThus, the number of distinct numbers in the list is \\(\\boxed{961}\\).",
